1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,575
Hi Mom, it's Arman, new number.

2
00:00:02,575 --> 00:00:06,300
Send eighty-five thousand to my friend's card, don't tell Dad.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,450
Every family in Kazakhstan has seen this message.

4
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:16,238
Now AI assistants are starting to pay bills and answer sellers for people.

5
00:00:16,238 --> 00:00:19,463
When that message reaches an agent, who stops the payment?

6
00:00:19,462 --> 00:00:24,000
This is MoneyGate: a safety gate for AI agents that move money.

7
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:27,062
The agent proposes one action.

8
00:00:27,062 --> 00:00:39,638
Before it runs, MoneyGate checks it three ways: a mandate with limits and hard rules, like never giving out an SMS code; a Muse Spark judge; and red-flag rules in Russian, Kazakh and English.

9
00:00:39,638 --> 00:00:44,688
Screenshots are read by Muse Spark, voice notes by Muse Voice Transcribe.

10
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:47,062
Here is the assistant in Telegram.

11
00:00:47,062 --> 00:00:50,000
I forward the screenshot and ask it to send the money.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,512
The agent proposes the transfer, exactly as asked.

13
00:00:53,512 --> 00:01:00,262
MoneyGate stops it: someone on a new number, a card from the message, pressure to hurry, keep it secret.

14
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,538
The same scam as a voice note in Kazakh.

15
00:01:17,538 --> 00:01:23,125
Meta's transcriber doesn't cover Kazakh yet, so MoneyGate falls back to Muse Spark audio.

16
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:26,362
Stopped again, and the advice comes back in Kazakh.

17
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:42,262
And an ordinary bill goes straight through.

18
00:01:42,262 --> 00:01:45,125
A gate that blocks everything is useless.

19
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:58,262
Every decision is written to a hash-chained journal.

20
00:01:58,262 --> 00:02:03,925
An independent tool verifies it, and if anyone edits a single record, the chain breaks.

21
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:15,988
We measured it.

22
00:02:15,988 --> 00:02:20,525
Muse Spark already knows scams: in plain chat it warns every time.

23
00:02:20,525 --> 00:02:22,763
But agents don't chat, they act.

24
00:02:22,762 --> 00:02:27,675
An agent that does what it's asked would lose money in forty-six of forty-eight cases.

25
00:02:27,675 --> 00:02:32,675
Even Muse Spark as the agent agreed once, to a Kazakh marketplace prepayment.

26
00:02:32,675 --> 00:02:37,150
A small on-device model warns in nine of thirty-six, never in Kazakh.

27
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:41,675
With MoneyGate: every scam stopped, no legitimate request blocked.

28
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:47,800
Any agent can call MoneyGate over MCP.

29
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:52,588
Muse Spark knows the scam; MoneyGate makes it a check no agent can skip.

30
00:02:52,588 --> 00:02:53,588
Try the bot.

31
00:02:53,588 --> 00:02:55,175
The code is on GitHub.
